{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     training/pace — the commitment, as a date rather than a number of hours.
     Ported from NS-Design-System/templates/training-index.html §05.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ DUMMY FIGURES. A marketing band, same as training/path and
     training/tiers — see the note at the top of training.hbs for why those
     three may hold copy and training/modules may not.

     "42 hours" is a number nobody can act on; "by 14 October" is a decision.
     That swap is the whole point of the band, and it is why the date is the
     largest thing in it.

     ⚠ --sunken IS PART OF THE PAGE'S RHYTHM, NOT DECORATION. The bands
     alternate default / sunken down the page, and demo-training-index.html
     runs: thero, band, SUNKEN, band, SUNKEN(tight), band, dark. Dropping
     --sunken here put three default-ground bands in a row — tiers, pace and
     people read as one long undifferentiated section with no seam, which is
     what "the spacing is wrong" actually looks like. It is not padding.

     ⚠ THE SEGMENTED CONTROL IS INERT HERE. Upstream's product version
     recomputes the date from the selected pace; this theme ships no script
     for it, so the radios change nothing. It is kept because it states the
     assumption the date rests on — "at 30 min a day" — which a bare date
     would hide. If it ever needs to compute, the behaviour is upstream in
     assets/js/training.js and this band should take that rather than grow
     its own.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight ns-band--sunken">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <div class="ns-pace ns-pace--inline">
            <div>
                <span class="ns-pace__label">{{t "Finish the foundations by"}}</span>
                <time class="ns-pace__date" datetime="2026-10-14">{{t "14 October 2026"}}</time>
                <span class="ns-pace__meta"><b>{{t "53 days at 30 min a day"}}</b><span>{{t "Read at whatever pace you actually keep"}}</span></span>
            </div>

            <fieldset class="ns-pace__control ns-bare">
                <legend class="ns-visually-hidden">{{t "How much time per day"}}</legend>
                <div class="ns-segmented">
                    <label class="ns-segmented__option"><input type="radio" name="training-pace" value="15"><span>{{t "15 min"}}</span></label>
                    <label class="ns-segmented__option"><input type="radio" name="training-pace" value="30" checked><span>{{t "30 min"}}</span></label>
                    <label class="ns-segmented__option"><input type="radio" name="training-pace" value="60"><span>{{t "1 hr"}}</span></label>
                </div>
            </fieldset>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
